\ Interpreter-free AOT dispatch through `tri`: a row-variable combinator with
\ three quotation parameters. The former strict-mode rejection of the dynamic
\ quotation call is lifted, so the compiled body dispatches to each parameter
\ quotation via its attached code_ptr (the caller's literal quotations compile).
\ A parameter with no compiled code_ptr would trap; here all three compile, so
\ the body runs interpreter-free and matches the interpreter.
1 [ 2 + ] [ 3 + ] [ 4 + ] tri . . .
